1
00:00:19,860 --> 00:00:24,260
Come to me, all you who have no money.

2
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:28,980
I don't have any either, but don't worry.

3
00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:36,040
Look at the blue sky and the white clouds.

4
00:00:36,040 --> 00:00:36,460
Me.

5
00:00:39,540 --> 00:00:43,000
Somehow it'll all work out, right?

6
00:00:55,960 --> 00:00:59,900
Come to me, all you who have no jobs.

7
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:04,520
I don't have any either, but don't worry.

8
00:01:04,520 --> 00:01:11,580
Look at the burning steel clouds.

9
00:01:13,380 --> 00:01:18,260
Somehow it'll all work
out eventually, right?

10
00:01:20,240 --> 00:01:23,540
You get it, right? Got it, got it.

11
00:01:23,540 --> 00:01:27,440
Once you understand, quietly follow me.

12
00:01:41,300 --> 00:01:43,860
Search high and low! The great chase!

13
00:01:49,940 --> 00:01:51,200
So, Ryotsu, what do you think?

14
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:52,540
This is terrible.

15
00:01:52,540 --> 00:01:54,880
The prongs on the setting
are about to come off.

16
00:01:54,880 --> 00:01:57,640
C'mon, can you fix it, Ryotsu?

17
00:01:58,140 --> 00:02:01,920
It's a precious ring I bought to
commemorate our 30th wedding anniversary.

18
00:02:01,920 --> 00:02:05,140
Your anniversary is the day after tomorrow,
isn't it?

19
00:02:05,140 --> 00:02:05,820
That's right.

20
00:02:06,260 --> 00:02:08,940
I was going to secretly give it
to my wife to surprise her, but

21
00:02:09,360 --> 00:02:10,560
I accidentally dropped it

22
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:11,720
and ended up stepping on it.

23
00:02:11,720 --> 00:02:15,060
If it's going to be ready by the day after tomorrow,
we have to rush the repair.

24
00:02:15,060 --> 00:02:16,840
If we're going to have
a professional shop do it,

25
00:02:16,840 --> 00:02:19,660
you'd better be prepared to
pay 100,000 yen for the repair.

26
00:02:19,660 --> 00:02:20,240
What?

27
00:02:20,740 --> 00:02:22,100
Is it really going to cost that much?

28
00:02:22,100 --> 00:02:25,080
This kind of work requires a lot of skill,
you know.

29
00:02:25,620 --> 00:02:26,380
Well, anyway,

30
00:02:26,380 --> 00:02:28,660
I'll have a workshop I know

31
00:02:28,660 --> 00:02:30,760
handle it for 30,000 yen.

32
00:02:32,200 --> 00:02:36,100
Thank goodness. Your wide network
actually comes in handy once in a while.

33
00:02:36,820 --> 00:02:37,460
Then here you go.

34
00:02:38,600 --> 00:02:42,780
Count on you, Ryotsu. No matter what, make
sure it's ready by the day after tomorrow.

35
00:02:42,780 --> 00:02:46,600
I know, I know. Trust me, will you? Buchuun!

36
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:50,520
I don't trust you one bit.
Nakagawa, I'm counting on you.

37
00:02:50,520 --> 00:02:53,440
Make sure Ryotsu keeps his promise.

38
00:02:53,440 --> 00:02:54,660
Yes, sir.

39
00:02:55,220 --> 00:02:58,200
Well then, Ryotsu.
I'm really counting on you.

40
00:02:58,200 --> 00:02:59,400
Leave it to me.

41
00:03:02,060 --> 00:03:04,860
You're saying I can't be trusted?

42
00:03:06,320 --> 00:03:09,360
Exactly! We're not going to hand
it to some outside repair shop!

43
00:03:09,500 --> 00:03:11,960
We'll fix it ourselves and
pocket the full 30,000 yen!

44
00:03:13,580 --> 00:03:15,000
Are you planning to swindle us again?

45
00:03:15,320 --> 00:03:19,540
It's fine! The Chief is thrilled it
only cost 30,000 instead of 100,000!

46
00:03:19,840 --> 00:03:21,320
Excuse me, coming in!

47
00:03:22,700 --> 00:03:23,140
What?

48
00:03:23,840 --> 00:03:26,980
Reiko's in the back making teddy bears!

49
00:03:27,840 --> 00:03:29,100
Teddy bears?

50
00:03:31,380 --> 00:03:32,980
She's pretty good at it.

51
00:03:33,660 --> 00:03:35,340
Don't disturb her, Ryo-chan.

52
00:03:35,940 --> 00:03:38,860
But why is she making
stuffed bears of all things?

53
00:03:39,260 --> 00:03:42,880
Apparently she's selling them at the Katsushika
police station's charity bazaar tomorrow.

54
00:03:48,760 --> 00:03:52,200
Anyway, how many of these
bears are you planning to make?

55
00:03:52,720 --> 00:03:55,200
I'm planning to make 200, for now.

56
00:03:55,200 --> 00:03:56,560
200?

57
00:03:56,560 --> 00:03:59,300
Reiko's teddy bears are really popular,
you know.

58
00:03:59,760 --> 00:04:01,680
They always sell out right away.

59
00:04:02,060 --> 00:04:04,840
Teddy bears have fans all over the world,

60
00:04:05,460 --> 00:04:09,380
and there's even a yearly contest where
people compete with their prized teddy bears.

61
00:04:10,040 --> 00:04:10,360
And that one?

62
00:04:13,560 --> 00:04:15,600
It's a bear belonging to a friend in France.

63
00:04:15,600 --> 00:04:18,600
It looks really old. It's falling apart!

64
00:04:18,940 --> 00:04:21,540
I'm going to take it apart
and remake it as good as new.

65
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:23,920
Why go to the trouble of doing that?

66
00:04:24,660 --> 00:04:25,880
You see, in Europe,

67
00:04:25,930 --> 00:04:29,320
when a baby is born,
people give them a teddy bear.

68
00:04:30,500 --> 00:04:32,820
At first, the bear is bigger than the child.

69
00:04:33,660 --> 00:04:35,370
But soon the child outgrows it,

70
00:04:35,420 --> 00:04:38,140
and they share many memories with the bear.

71
00:04:38,620 --> 00:04:41,660
Then, when they get married, they take
the bear along with their furniture,

72
00:04:41,660 --> 00:04:44,720
and let their own children play with it.

73
00:04:46,940 --> 00:04:50,660
I see, so one teddy bear gets passed down
through generations of parents and children.

74
00:04:51,304 --> 00:04:54,740
Isn't the stuffing inside cotton?

75
00:04:55,500 --> 00:04:56,961
It's called "pan-ya" (Panya).

76
00:04:57,011 --> 00:05:00,940
Apparently it's fiber that wraps
the seeds of a plant called kapok.

77
00:05:01,160 --> 00:05:04,000
What are these little granules?

78
00:05:04,340 --> 00:05:07,195
They're pellets. To balance the weight,

79
00:05:07,245 --> 00:05:09,280
they're packed inside along with the kapok.

80
00:05:09,440 --> 00:05:11,220
I see. So that's what it is.

81
00:05:13,653 --> 00:05:16,346
They don't look much different
from the gems in the Chief's ring.

82
00:05:16,396 --> 00:05:19,140
If we swapped them,
wouldn't he never notice?

83
00:05:20,660 --> 00:05:25,020
Your eyes are like knotholes,
and you've been babbling for a while now.

84
00:05:25,020 --> 00:05:29,660
You're noisy, and frankly, you're in the way.
It's like having a beast among beauties.

85
00:05:29,660 --> 00:05:32,340
ばかりのところに野獣が一匹いる って感じ

86
00:05:33,060 --> 00:05:38,220
Yeah, sorry for being a beast, I'll have you know.
And you two aren't beauties at all either.

87
00:05:38,220 --> 00:05:39,900
Hey, what did you just say?

88
00:05:39,900 --> 00:05:42,260
Let's go, Nakagawa.
Y-yes!

89
00:05:42,660 --> 00:05:45,920
Nakagawa's fine. He can stay.

90
00:05:46,380 --> 00:05:49,780
What, so I'm the only one in the way?
Well, obviously.

91
00:05:50,660 --> 00:05:52,960
If you help out too, Ryo-chan, you can stay.

92
00:05:53,380 --> 00:05:58,000
No thanks.
I've got better-paying work to do. See ya.

93
00:05:58,480 --> 00:06:01,820
Hmph. Don't take Nakagawa with you.

94
00:06:02,360 --> 00:06:03,920
No way! Bleh!

95
00:06:04,960 --> 00:06:05,900
Geez, you're so stingy.

96
00:06:17,640 --> 00:06:19,760
Thank you, please love it well.

97
00:06:19,760 --> 00:06:20,280
Yeah.

98
00:06:20,280 --> 00:06:22,160
Isn't that great, Saki-chan.

99
00:06:22,160 --> 00:06:23,760
It's Mom.

100
00:06:23,760 --> 00:06:24,500
Thank you very much.

101
00:06:26,300 --> 00:06:28,640
Going well, aren't they? How many are left?

102
00:06:30,120 --> 00:06:32,260
Ten left, we're almost there.

103
00:06:32,260 --> 00:06:34,860
At this rate, we'll sell out in an hour.

104
00:06:40,420 --> 00:06:43,580
Every bazaar this year is doing pretty well

105
00:06:43,580 --> 00:06:44,300
Yeah, that's right.

106
00:06:45,920 --> 00:06:46,320
Yes.

107
00:06:48,300 --> 00:06:48,900
Ryotsu

108
00:06:48,900 --> 00:06:50,180
Chief.

109
00:06:50,180 --> 00:06:51,820
Is the ring all right?

110
00:06:51,820 --> 00:06:52,960
The ring?

111
00:06:52,960 --> 00:06:54,720
Hey, the ring.

112
00:06:55,280 --> 00:06:57,260
You haven't forgotten it, have you?

113
00:06:57,260 --> 00:06:59,920
Well, I'm having it checked
by a jeweler I know right now.

114
00:06:59,920 --> 00:07:03,180
You're really sure you can finish
the repair by tomorrow, right?

115
00:07:03,740 --> 00:07:05,900
Well, Chief, you do worry a lot.

116
00:07:05,900 --> 00:07:07,380
Leave it to me.

117
00:07:08,140 --> 00:07:09,140
What's wrong, Ryotsu?

118
00:07:09,140 --> 00:07:11,120
No, it's nothing.

119
00:07:11,940 --> 00:07:14,040
My phone's battery died.

120
00:07:15,600 --> 00:07:17,840
Senpai, what happened to the ring?

121
00:07:18,320 --> 00:07:19,240
I don't know.

122
00:07:19,240 --> 00:07:21,460
I was planning to work
on it a little tonight,

123
00:07:21,460 --> 00:07:23,540
but I never even took it out of the box.

124
00:07:23,540 --> 00:07:25,140
Where did it go?

125
00:07:25,140 --> 00:07:26,880
Not once.

126
00:07:27,500 --> 00:07:28,880
Senpai, could it be...

127
00:07:28,880 --> 00:07:31,460
when Reiko was making
the teddy bears yesterday?

128
00:07:33,180 --> 00:07:37,680
It's like there's a beast in there...
those little pellets

129
00:07:38,780 --> 00:07:43,120
Hurry, to Reiko's room!
That's the place. Thank you very much.

130
00:07:43,120 --> 00:07:43,580
Thank you very much.

131
00:07:45,200 --> 00:07:46,260
What is it?

132
00:07:47,980 --> 00:07:49,820
Reiko, about the teddy bears...

133
00:07:49,820 --> 00:07:52,540
Ryo-chan, did you want a teddy bear too?

134
00:07:53,020 --> 00:07:54,740
It's not that kind of situation!

135
00:07:54,740 --> 00:07:56,760
Where is it? Where is it?

136
00:07:57,220 --> 00:08:00,940
Sorry, the last one just sold out.

137
00:08:03,760 --> 00:08:05,160
We're too late, damn it!

138
00:08:06,340 --> 00:08:07,760
What do we do now, Senpai?

139
00:08:08,200 --> 00:08:10,960
Chief's ring is inside one of those.

140
00:08:10,960 --> 00:08:12,840
I don't know what you're talking about,

141
00:08:12,840 --> 00:08:16,420
but I have the addresses of
everyone who bought a bear.

142
00:08:16,420 --> 00:08:17,300
Really?

143
00:08:17,300 --> 00:08:19,500
Yes! You're amazing, Reiko-con!

144
00:08:19,500 --> 00:08:21,320
Stop it, Ryo-chan.

145
00:08:21,320 --> 00:08:26,240
I've entered 200 people's
details into this computer.

146
00:08:26,240 --> 00:08:28,280
It's for aftercare too,

147
00:08:28,280 --> 00:08:30,680
so I had everyone sign up as members.

148
00:08:30,680 --> 00:08:33,080
Right, with this data,

149
00:08:33,080 --> 00:08:36,860
but earlier you were saying something about the Chief.
What's going on?

150
00:08:38,940 --> 00:08:41,020
Well, that's

151
00:08:41,940 --> 00:08:44,680
Reiko, there's actually something
important I need to tell you.

152
00:08:44,680 --> 00:08:46,140
What is it?

153
00:08:46,880 --> 00:08:47,220
Yes?

154
00:08:47,220 --> 00:08:49,683
What's squid called in French?

155
00:08:49,733 --> 00:08:51,860
Is it "ashi jupon"?

156
00:08:51,960 --> 00:08:52,980
It's "calamar."

157
00:08:52,980 --> 00:08:53,880
Uh-huh, and octopus?

158
00:08:54,040 --> 00:08:55,000
I think it's "poulpe."

159
00:08:58,340 --> 00:08:59,900
We've got the buyer list!

160
00:09:00,120 --> 00:09:02,660
The ring must be inside
one of these teddy bears!

161
00:09:06,860 --> 00:09:07,160
Yes.

162
00:09:07,660 --> 00:09:09,280
We're with the police.

163
00:09:09,280 --> 00:09:09,840
Yes.

164
00:09:10,600 --> 00:09:11,480
What is it?

165
00:09:11,980 --> 00:09:15,560
Ma'am, you bought a teddy bear at the charity bazaar,
didn't you?

166
00:09:15,560 --> 00:09:17,260
Yes, what about it?

167
00:09:17,260 --> 00:09:18,880
Actually, inside it

168
00:09:18,880 --> 00:09:22,080
we've received information
that drugs are hidden in it.

169
00:09:23,560 --> 00:09:24,520
Senpai.

170
00:09:24,520 --> 00:09:26,520
Could we take a look?

171
00:09:26,520 --> 00:09:27,520
Yes, right away.

172
00:09:28,180 --> 00:09:30,540
Is it all right to say something like that?

173
00:09:30,540 --> 00:09:32,980
Well, we can't exactly
tell the truth, can we?

174
00:09:35,120 --> 00:09:36,120
Did you find it?

175
00:09:36,860 --> 00:09:39,080
It's just stuffing.

176
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:41,400
Next one! Hurry!

177
00:09:41,520 --> 00:09:45,160
Uh-oh, here comes Bear-chan!

178
00:09:45,160 --> 00:09:48,200
We're animal doctors, sweetie.

179
00:09:48,200 --> 00:09:50,460
We'll put it back together right away.

180
00:09:50,460 --> 00:09:51,500
Did you find it?

181
00:09:51,800 --> 00:09:52,540
No, we didn't.

182
00:09:54,380 --> 00:09:54,820
Yes.

183
00:09:54,820 --> 00:09:56,760
We're with the police.

184
00:09:56,760 --> 00:09:59,020
The thing is, there's
Translation>
inside that teddy bear

185
00:09:59,020 --> 00:10:01,520
we've received a tip that
drugs are hidden in it.

186
00:10:01,520 --> 00:10:02,260
Really?

187
00:10:03,040 --> 00:10:06,140
But I bought this one fifteen years ago.

188
00:10:06,140 --> 00:10:06,560
What?

189
00:10:07,280 --> 00:10:09,640
Are there other teddy bears?

190
00:10:10,080 --> 00:10:10,480
Yes.

191
00:10:18,340 --> 00:10:19,740
Roughly 3,000 yen.

192
00:10:19,740 --> 00:10:23,340
The one we bought today should
be in here somewhere too.

193
00:10:24,340 --> 00:10:26,680
There really are people like this,
aren't there.

194
00:10:26,680 --> 00:10:29,300
Looks like we have no choice
but to find it among these.

195
00:10:29,760 --> 00:10:30,160
Yeah.

196
00:10:31,400 --> 00:10:33,580
Phew, this one spot alone took an hour!

197
00:10:33,580 --> 00:10:34,760
Hurry up, Nakagawa!

198
00:10:41,160 --> 00:10:43,432
So you're Sayuri Arisugawa,
the gray-haired Nese type.

199
00:10:43,482 --> 00:10:45,640
My gut says this one's suspicious.

200
00:10:45,820 --> 00:10:46,920
Coming!

201
00:10:48,060 --> 00:10:50,600
Yes, it's Sayuri~!

202
00:10:52,360 --> 00:10:54,140
Well, this one is more my taste.

203
00:10:55,340 --> 00:10:57,000
What's this about?

204
00:10:57,220 --> 00:10:59,300
Nakagawa, hurry and check that room.

205
00:10:59,380 --> 00:11:01,740
This crunchy-headed one is irresistible.

206
00:11:01,740 --> 00:11:02,740
Nakagawa.

207
00:11:03,180 --> 00:11:03,820
Yes.

208
00:11:04,120 --> 00:11:07,280
Nakagawa, still, come on, hurry up.

209
00:11:11,020 --> 00:11:12,000
Irresistible

210
00:11:12,700 --> 00:11:14,100
How many is that now?

211
00:11:14,580 --> 00:11:16,560
I've only checked seven so far.

212
00:11:16,560 --> 00:11:19,120
There are still 193 more?

213
00:11:19,120 --> 00:11:20,780
Anyway, let's hurry.

214
00:11:25,680 --> 00:11:28,940
About that teddy bear...

215
00:11:28,940 --> 00:11:30,660
Well, do come in.

216
00:11:35,240 --> 00:11:39,340
That teddy bear was bought by my grandson,
you see.

217
00:11:41,920 --> 00:11:45,000
He seemed to like it very much.

218
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:46,880
So, where is your grandson now?

219
00:11:48,260 --> 00:11:52,920
He just left with his parents a moment ago.

220
00:11:53,540 --> 00:11:58,400
It's become so lonely,
as if the fire has gone out.

221
00:11:58,400 --> 00:12:00,000
Left? Where to?

222
00:12:03,580 --> 00:12:05,980
Yes, by bullet train.

223
00:12:05,980 --> 00:12:07,060
By bullet train?

224
00:12:07,060 --> 00:12:09,220
To Atami.

225
00:12:11,020 --> 00:12:11,220
Yes.

226
00:12:11,780 --> 00:12:14,460
From there, take a ferry to Oshima.

227
00:12:14,460 --> 00:12:15,000
Hey, you!

228
00:12:15,220 --> 00:12:15,720
Senpai!

229
00:12:16,720 --> 00:12:18,120
To Oshima! Hurry!

230
00:12:18,340 --> 00:12:18,700
Yes.

231
00:12:19,280 --> 00:12:22,220
Do you have a photo or
something of your grandson?

232
00:12:24,740 --> 00:12:27,980
Making us wait thirty minutes
just to find a photo, geez!

233
00:12:29,060 --> 00:12:31,180
Damn it!
In that case, we're using our trump card!

234
00:12:33,700 --> 00:12:34,700
S-senpai!

235
00:12:34,820 --> 00:12:36,240
Just go at full power!

236
00:12:36,340 --> 00:12:37,880
We have to catch up to the bullet train!

237
00:12:38,200 --> 00:12:38,560
Yes!

238
00:12:54,080 --> 00:12:56,340
Thank you for watching.

239
00:13:15,120 --> 00:13:16,300
The gate is closing.

240
00:13:16,300 --> 00:13:17,180
Go for it!

241
00:13:27,340 --> 00:13:29,940
Honestly, Senpai, you're so reckless.

242
00:13:29,940 --> 00:13:31,500
Forget that, the teddy bear!

243
00:13:41,940 --> 00:13:44,540
Where's the teddy bear,
where's the teddy bear?

244
00:13:44,720 --> 00:13:46,440
Senpai, over there!

245
00:13:48,440 --> 00:13:50,000
That ferry over there?

246
00:13:53,460 --> 00:13:56,240
Damn it! We've come all this way,
we can't let him get away!

247
00:13:56,640 --> 00:14:00,400
Senpai!

248
00:14:02,520 --> 00:14:05,020
Hey! Ferry! Wait up!

249
00:14:06,640 --> 00:14:08,300
That's sheer determination!

250
00:14:13,780 --> 00:14:16,280
Not here, not here, not here.

251
00:14:16,280 --> 00:14:18,200
Oh no, what a disaster.

252
00:14:18,200 --> 00:14:24,540
It's not here, is it?

253
00:14:24,580 --> 00:14:26,900
Damn it, next one!

254
00:14:44,080 --> 00:14:46,640
Why is it taking so long to find it?

255
00:14:46,640 --> 00:14:48,980
That makes 199 bears so far.

256
00:14:48,980 --> 00:14:54,220
That means it's definitely inside
the last remaining teddy bear.

257
00:14:55,520 --> 00:14:58,320
Minato Ward, Aoyama, M Christie.

258
00:14:58,320 --> 00:14:59,960
She's a foreign woman, isn't she?

259
00:14:59,960 --> 00:15:03,460
She's not that French friend
Reiko mentioned, is she?

260
00:15:04,040 --> 00:15:05,760
I've got a bad feeling about this.

261
00:15:06,660 --> 00:15:08,320
She went back to France?

262
00:15:09,320 --> 00:15:11,340
Yes, on the 4 o'clock flight.

263
00:15:11,340 --> 00:15:12,760
Narita! Hurry!

264
00:15:18,200 --> 00:15:20,580
It's almost takeoff time. You won't make it.

265
00:15:20,580 --> 00:15:22,840
No matter what, I'll make it in time.

266
00:15:35,920 --> 00:15:36,680
Captain

267
00:15:36,680 --> 00:15:41,320
We've received word from the control tower
that a bomb has been planted on this aircraft.

268
00:15:41,320 --> 00:15:41,820
What?

269
00:15:42,260 --> 00:15:43,280
Halt the aircraft.

270
00:15:52,020 --> 00:15:53,600
We apologize for the inconvenience.

271
00:15:53,980 --> 00:15:57,240
This aircraft will be undergoing
an emergency inspection.

272
00:15:57,760 --> 00:16:01,240
Passengers, please return to
your seats and wait a moment.

273
00:16:04,980 --> 00:16:08,040
Senpai, is it really all right to do this?

274
00:16:08,040 --> 00:16:10,120
Whether it's all right or not,
this is an emergency.

275
00:16:10,120 --> 00:16:14,820
If we don't find the ring, even Nakagawa
won't have a face to show the Chief, will he?

276
00:16:16,360 --> 00:16:20,480
Everyone, please follow the
instructions of the bomb disposal unit.

277
00:16:21,660 --> 00:16:23,800
What do you mean, a bomb?

278
00:16:24,440 --> 00:16:26,000
Please stay calm.

279
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:29,140
Someone here has a teddy bear, right?

280
00:16:29,140 --> 00:16:31,280
There's a bomb inside it...

281
00:16:34,800 --> 00:16:35,480
What is this?

282
00:16:36,380 --> 00:16:37,420
W-well...

283
00:16:37,420 --> 00:16:38,076
This bottle...

284
00:16:38,126 --> 00:16:41,940
It's a private charter for a tour heading
to the world teddy bear competition.

285
00:16:42,700 --> 00:16:44,800
Don't make things more
complicated than they need to be!

286
00:16:45,380 --> 00:16:47,020
Senpai, what should we do?

287
00:16:47,500 --> 00:16:49,380
I know whose teddy bear it is.

288
00:16:49,380 --> 00:16:51,840
Find the French woman, Christy!

289
00:16:55,300 --> 00:16:56,040
Interesting.

290
00:17:03,540 --> 00:17:04,340
That's the one!

291
00:17:06,020 --> 00:17:08,360
The one Reiko was fixing back then.

292
00:17:08,360 --> 00:17:09,060
Thank goodness.

293
00:17:09,700 --> 00:17:11,520
Bring that teddy bear over here.

294
00:17:11,520 --> 00:17:13,820
This one stinks.

295
00:17:13,820 --> 00:17:15,240
How did you figure that out?

296
00:17:15,880 --> 00:17:16,520
What?

297
00:17:16,520 --> 00:17:17,280
Senior officer.

298
00:17:17,740 --> 00:17:18,380
Don't move.

299
00:17:18,380 --> 00:17:21,280
If you move, I'll turn on the bomb's switch.

300
00:17:24,960 --> 00:17:26,560
I told you not to move.

301
00:17:26,560 --> 00:17:30,580
Once the switch is on, this bomb
goes off in ten seconds, understand?

302
00:17:31,620 --> 00:17:32,260
N-no way...

303
00:17:32,260 --> 00:17:35,360
I can't believe there's
a real bomb in there.

304
00:17:35,820 --> 00:17:36,620
Ladies and gentlemen,

305
00:17:36,620 --> 00:17:39,300
if you don't do as you're told,
it's going to go boom!

306
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:49,660
Thanks for coming all this way.

307
00:17:49,660 --> 00:17:51,720
But we don't need you two.

308
00:17:52,080 --> 00:17:52,600
Raid!

309
00:17:52,600 --> 00:18:06,060
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

310
00:18:09,860 --> 00:18:12,800
We finally found the teddy bear we were after,
and yet...

311
00:18:12,800 --> 00:18:14,520
Why is our luck so terrible?

312
00:18:16,600 --> 00:18:21,620
Ken-chan.

313
00:18:21,620 --> 00:18:24,140
Nakagawa, what on earth is going on?

314
00:18:24,560 --> 00:18:27,180
The Chief is on that plane...

315
00:18:27,670 --> 00:18:28,440
Ryo-chan is...

316
00:18:29,100 --> 00:18:31,140
What is the culprit demanding?

317
00:18:32,240 --> 00:18:32,800
That's...

318
00:18:33,920 --> 00:18:36,720
I really hate teddy bears.

319
00:18:37,400 --> 00:18:41,060
So, all of you, bring every teddy
bear you have to the cargo hold.

320
00:18:41,060 --> 00:18:43,420
Then we'll throw them all
into the sea from there.

321
00:18:44,760 --> 00:18:48,700
What a lunatic,
hijacking a plane for something like that!

322
00:18:48,700 --> 00:18:50,840
But why teddy bears?

323
00:18:51,420 --> 00:18:52,620
I don't know.

324
00:18:53,380 --> 00:18:55,500
Now we're counting on Ryotsu.

325
00:18:56,040 --> 00:18:59,248
But Senpai isn't on the plane,

326
00:18:59,298 --> 00:19:00,640
he's outside.

327
00:19:02,680 --> 00:19:04,400
My hands are going numb.

328
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:08,100
Hurry up and throw your teddy bears away!

329
00:19:09,220 --> 00:19:10,540
My Bear-chan!

330
00:19:10,540 --> 00:19:12,000
Don't dawdle!

331
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:15,340
Why do I have to throw away my Bear-chan?

332
00:19:16,960 --> 00:19:18,460
Then I'll tell you.

333
00:19:18,460 --> 00:19:22,200
My name is Teddy Kumao.

334
00:19:25,560 --> 00:19:27,280
How cute.

335
00:19:27,940 --> 00:19:29,440
Shut up, shut up, shut up!

336
00:19:30,640 --> 00:19:32,540
You bastards will never
understand how I feel!

337
00:19:33,200 --> 00:19:36,980
"Teddy bear, teddy bear"...
I've been mocked for that since I was a kid!

338
00:19:37,260 --> 00:19:41,000
If teddy bears had never existed in this world,
my life wouldn't have turned out like this!

339
00:19:46,940 --> 00:19:49,900
That was my fourth birthday.

340
00:19:50,840 --> 00:19:54,200
All my relatives gathered
and gave me presents.

341
00:19:54,800 --> 00:19:57,020
And every single one was a teddy bear!

342
00:19:57,740 --> 00:19:59,740
They all picked them because of my name,

343
00:19:59,740 --> 00:20:01,680
and they thoughtlessly ruined the presents!

344
00:20:02,240 --> 00:20:03,740
Ever since then, my life

345
00:20:03,740 --> 00:20:05,600
has been nothing but failure,
no matter what I do.

346
00:20:05,980 --> 00:20:07,360
My job hunt came in dead last,

347
00:20:07,360 --> 00:20:08,420
I flunked university,

348
00:20:08,420 --> 00:20:09,560
and I can't even get married.

349
00:20:09,560 --> 00:20:12,620
W-wait,
that's not the teddy bears' fault at all!

350
00:20:13,560 --> 00:20:16,120
No, I'm cursed by teddy bears.

351
00:20:16,480 --> 00:20:17,560
Even my life reading

352
00:20:17,560 --> 00:20:19,220
says my fortune is the worst!

353
00:20:19,220 --> 00:20:20,620
This is ridiculous!

354
00:20:20,620 --> 00:20:21,140
Shut up.

355
00:20:21,140 --> 00:20:24,040
Captain, open the cargo hold.

356
00:20:24,040 --> 00:20:25,000
Hurry up.

357
00:20:25,780 --> 00:20:27,360
Mm... there's no choice.

358
00:20:37,640 --> 00:20:39,700
Now the time for revenge has come!

359
00:20:41,720 --> 00:20:44,480
Damn it, if it's come to this,
it's stone or Bajika!

360
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:46,080
Here goes!

361
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:56,460
This teddy bear is Reiko's!

362
00:20:57,400 --> 00:20:58,340
W-what happened?

363
00:21:02,480 --> 00:21:04,800
Found it! We finally got it back!

364
00:21:07,500 --> 00:21:08,960
The real one is this one.

365
00:21:09,880 --> 00:21:12,460
No, the one I was looking for is this one.

366
00:21:13,240 --> 00:21:15,240
This is no time to be saying that!

367
00:21:15,920 --> 00:21:18,560
If you try anything funny,
I'll flip the bomb's switch!

368
00:21:19,040 --> 00:21:20,480
W-wait! Calm down!

369
00:21:21,100 --> 00:21:23,980
Ryotsu! Don't excite the suspect!

370
00:21:26,180 --> 00:21:27,860
Ugh...

371
00:21:27,860 --> 00:21:29,820
Senpai!

372
00:21:32,580 --> 00:21:35,040
Damn it, we have to do something!

373
00:21:35,880 --> 00:21:38,760
Come on,
if you touch that bear with your hand...

374
00:21:38,760 --> 00:21:40,020
Aaargh!

375
00:21:41,020 --> 00:21:41,880
What!

376
00:21:42,020 --> 00:21:45,100
No! Ah! Aaah!

377
00:21:45,380 --> 00:21:46,560
Gaaaah!

378
00:21:52,480 --> 00:21:54,160
Hurry up and throw it away!

379
00:21:58,280 --> 00:21:59,440
Wait, this is...

380
00:22:08,560 --> 00:22:10,020
Serves you right!

381
00:22:10,020 --> 00:22:12,360
The teddy bear with the bomb inside

382
00:22:12,360 --> 00:22:14,440
Nice, the switch is

383
00:22:22,140 --> 00:22:23,720
Oh no, there's no time left!

384
00:22:26,600 --> 00:22:28,500
Damn, the ring!

385
00:22:32,920 --> 00:22:34,040
Thank goodness.

386
00:22:35,200 --> 00:22:36,660
Not good.

387
00:22:40,280 --> 00:22:41,120
Ryo-chan

388
00:22:41,120 --> 00:22:41,700
Senpai

389
00:22:41,700 --> 00:22:43,480
Ry-Ryotsu, are you all right?

390
00:22:50,560 --> 00:22:51,680
Look.

391
00:22:53,500 --> 00:22:54,480
He's safe.

392
00:22:58,720 --> 00:23:01,940
Well done, well done, Ryotsu!

393
00:23:07,880 --> 00:23:10,700
The ring, the ring!

394
00:23:10,700 --> 00:23:14,660
So now we search this entire sea?

395
00:23:21,600 --> 00:23:23,780
Looks like it's been cleanly repaired

396
00:23:23,780 --> 00:23:25,460
That's great, Chief.

397
00:23:25,460 --> 00:23:27,120
Good work, Ryotsu.

398
00:23:28,480 --> 00:23:31,220
I'm glad the ring was found, Nakagawa.

399
00:23:31,800 --> 00:23:33,680
We really went through a lot.

400
00:23:34,260 --> 00:23:36,480
Nakagawa Salvage went all out

401
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:39,980
and searched that vast sea for a tiny ring.

402
00:23:40,720 --> 00:23:42,440
Mobilizing a total of ten thousand people,

403
00:23:42,440 --> 00:23:44,980
it was a massive search
that cost billions of yen.

404
00:23:45,740 --> 00:23:48,520
But finding it in a single day is a miracle.

405
00:23:49,980 --> 00:23:52,660
A ring worth billions of yen in total

406
00:23:52,660 --> 00:23:55,900
Only the Chief doesn't know

407
00:24:12,920 --> 00:24:18,740
Na na na na, na na na na, na na na na

408
00:24:18,740 --> 00:24:24,220
to those who play a
foolish game with their looks

409
00:24:24,220 --> 00:24:27,400
I probably don't want to become that

410
00:24:27,400 --> 00:24:32,000
if you're dawdling around the corner

411
00:24:32,000 --> 00:24:34,320
the moon has run away

412
00:24:34,320 --> 00:24:38,000
because now isn't everything

413
00:24:38,000 --> 00:24:39,480
this crying voice of now

414
00:24:39,480 --> 00:24:42,540
don't get too worked up about it

415
00:24:42,540 --> 00:24:46,300
even if you tell a little
lie or cheat a little

416
00:24:46,880 --> 00:24:50,440
sometimes when you're helping someone

417
00:24:50,440 --> 00:24:52,440
Baby, do you know me?

418
00:24:52,520 --> 00:24:56,800
facing tomorrow with a nice spirit

419
00:24:57,980 --> 00:25:01,820
Don't lose heart, we'll do what needs doing.

420
00:25:01,820 --> 00:25:04,280
A cute spirit.

421
00:25:04,280 --> 00:25:07,680
What's hard to see is

422
00:25:08,840 --> 00:25:11,480
just because we want it to look that way.

423
00:25:11,480 --> 00:25:17,240
It's better than just a
surface makeover, right?

424
00:25:19,120 --> 00:25:23,580
Na na na na na na na na na na na na na.

425
00:25:28,500 --> 00:25:31,380
March 3rd is my birthday.

426
00:25:31,380 --> 00:25:34,680
But on this very day,
misfortune falls upon me.

427
00:25:34,680 --> 00:25:39,200
I'd decided that if it came to this, I
wouldn't set foot outside the car all day today.

428
00:25:39,200 --> 00:25:43,580
Why am I handcuffed to a truck,
driving through the northern country?

429
00:25:44,180 --> 00:25:48,180
Next time:
"Miserable Birthday, Again." See you then!

430
00:25:52,440 --> 00:25:52,800
Thank you.

431
00:25:52,800 --> 00:25:54,120
Be sure to catch us on camera.

432
00:25:54,120 --> 00:25:59,260
Everyone, come on over to our town!

433
00:26:00,180 --> 00:26:00,860
Thank you!

